            ---                                                                 
                                                                                
            Build a WSGI-compatible URL routing and view dispatching layer in   
            Python 3.11.                                                        
            The implementation must support: (1) URL resolution from a declared 
            list of                                                             
            patterns, including literal paths, variable segments with typed     
            converters for                                                      
            integers, strings, slugs, UUIDs and whole paths, and                
            regular-expression                                                  
            patterns with named groups; (2) request object encapsulating method,
            path,                                                               
            headers, query string, and body, with any segments captured from the
            URL                                                                 
            passed to the view; (3) view dispatch, in which the first matching  
            pattern's                                                           
            view is called with the request and the captured segments, and a    
            request                                                             
            matching no pattern yields a 404; (4) response handling, with a     
            response                                                            
            object carrying status code, headers, and body; (5) class-based     
            views, in                                                           
            which a view class dispatches a request to a method named for the   
            HTTP verb,                                                          
            returns 405 with an `Allow` header for a verb it does not implement,
            and                                                                 
            serves HEAD from the GET implementation. The implementation must    
            pass a WSGI                                                         
            compliance check. Provide a complete `pyproject.toml` and a         
