            path, headers, query string, and body\\n- URL segments captured from
            patterns are passed to views\\n- Query parameter parsing\\n- Header 
            normalization\\n\\n### 3. View Dispatch\\n- Function-based views    
            with captured URL parameters\\n- First matching pattern\'s view is  
            called\\n- 404 response for unmatched requests\\n\\n### 4. Response 
            Handling\\n- Response objects with status code, headers, and        
            body\\n- JSON response support\\n- Proper HTTP status codes and     
            headers\\n\\n### 5. Class-Based Views\\n- Method dispatch based on  
            HTTP verb (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, etc.)\\n- 405 Method Not Allowed 
            with proper `Allow` header for unsupported verbs\\n- HEAD requests  
            automatically served from GET implementation\\n- Template and       
            redirect view base classes\\n\\n## Installation\\n\\n```bash\\npip  
            install djangoframework\\n```\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### Basic    
            Usage\\n\\n```python\\nfrom djangoframework import (\\n             
            HttpRequest, HttpResponse, path, get_wsgi_application,              
            View\\n)\\n\\n# Function-based view\\ndef hello_world(request):\\n  
            return HttpResponse(\\"Hello, World!\\")\\n\\ndef                   
